# The first review gate, before any workflow runs.
#
# Turn this on under Settings → Branches → main → "Require review from Code
# Owners". Until then this file is documentation; with it, the paths below
# cannot reach main without the named reviewer, which is what makes the
# auto-apply on merge safe: everything that applies itself was reviewed here.

# Everything, by default.
*                           @spawan1998

# Infrastructure applies itself on merge. This is the review that matters.
/infra/terraform/           @spawan1998

# The intent file is the input to environment sizing and cost. A change here
# changes what gets provisioned and what it costs.
/platform.yaml              @spawan1998

# The pipeline's own rules -- including the approval gates. Without an owner
# here, a PR could remove its own reviewer requirement.
/.github/workflows/         @spawan1998
/.github/CODEOWNERS         @spawan1998

# The policy engine is the half of the AI layer that *decides*. The model's
# proposals are bounded by this file; weakening it weakens every guardrail.
/ai/aiops/policy.py         @spawan1998
